          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "CDIAL lists ਬੱਚਾ (bachchā) under Sanskrit apatya, \"offspring\", through Prakrit avacca (CDIAL 424), and its addenda set the word beside Persian bachcha, \"young (of humans or animals)\" (CDIAL 14226). Many take it from Persian instead, so its origin is not settled."
            }
          ]
        },
