        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ਆਦਮੀ (ādmī) is a loan from Arabic ādamī, \"human, of Adam\", which reached Punjabi through Persian. Its Arabic root is ʾ-d-m (Lane). It is Ādam, \"Adam\", with the Arabic ending -ī, \"belonging to\"."
            }
          ]
        },
